From 67e353a64ec4cd57ba4227e7e36d3acce6731b4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:21:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): describe held cards from their containment
 episode; wake or escalate once the authority finished [daveey]

A card that contained itself sits in triage with containment_episode set. kanban_wait_info described it from an older
park event (intake triage, not agent-owned), so the owner wake never fired, and the triage sweep skips held cards.
5 of the 6 contained cards on the hub (11-19/20) stranded this way: the named authority had completed or been
archived without releasing (plan review t_eeeeee000000001d, F3).

- kanban_contained_wait.read: per held triage card, the unreleased episode (kanban_containment_state.reduce_events),
  authority/producer status (board file, else Board replica; unknown counts as open) and when the authority finished.
- kanban_wait_info.describe_contained: wait.contained = {episode, authority: {id, status}, producer: {id, status}|None}.
  Authority open or producer open: not agent-owned. Authority done/archived 30+ min and no open producer: agent-owned,
  certain, stalled at once, dated from the authority's completion; premise = (contained, episode, authority status,
  authority completion), so the existing owner wake fires once per episode per authority completion.
- sweep_stale_triage: a stranded held card with no chat link gets one supervisor card, key
  containment-strand:<task>:<episode>, plus a comment on the held card; no event on the held card.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_contained_strand.py (RED on main: 9 of 10 fail; GREEN here). 20 files importing
the touched modules pass (469 tests). scripts/check --base origin/main ok.

Not in this change: the hermes-mods owner_wake.py wake text for contained cards (names the authority exits) and
remote rows: describe_replica reads card["contained"] when a projection supplies it; no projection fills it yet.
